      "message": "[warning] Line 70: 🟡 `addedDate` is assigned `Date(0)` whenever `added`/`addedMs` is present but parses to unknown (`0L`). That turns malformed/unknown metadata into a concrete epoch date instead of “no date”, and can leak into non-UI consumers (e.g., event ordering/timestamps) as a real value. Treat non-positive parsed values as absent (`null`) just like `removedDate` does, e.g. `addedDate \u003d TimestampUtils.fromDetails(details, \"added\").takeIf { it \u003e 0 }?.let(::Date)`.",
